Z||000000||fldevel||04-25-2001||05:55 PM||||how do you ppl get ur exhaust tips clean ?..i cant seem to get them to shine no matter how hard i try ?? any tips? "no pun intended"||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||04-25-2001||05:57 PM||||be lazy like me and just buy new ones!||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-25-2001||06:05 PM||||I prefer Brasso polish and Elbow brand Grease to keep my shiny stuff sparkly!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000003||banditbalz||04-25-2001||06:24 PM||||I use a product called "NeverDull". It looks like cotton Batten, but has a mild solvent mixed in. I spend half an hour every spring and it makes my tips look brand new. It's a very fine aggregate that you polish on and wipe off. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000004||MotherGoose||04-25-2001||06:33 PM||||This girl I know, then I just get them re-cromed. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000005||Phil||04-25-2001||06:43 PM||||Why chrome stainless just polish it||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||04-25-2001||06:54 PM||||Mother's Aluminum Wheel Polish.<BR>This stuff is great! If they are really dirty, clean them with Brasso first then polish with Mother's for a chrome like finish.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||04-25-2001||08:41 PM||||Try a product called Wenol.<BR>It blows Neverdul,Brasso and all the others<BR>listed above away!!<BR>You can only get it from Summit Racing.<BR>I have used all the above listed products<BR>and more but have NEVER found anything better! Nuy the metal polish not the auto.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fyerstarter||04-25-2001||10:08 PM||||When I first got my GT the exhaust tips were completely black. I used sandpaper to get rid of the layer of crap stuck on them (first 800 grit, then 1200, 1500, 1500 wet. Then mothers polish.<P>Course it was all for naught because I bought new cooler exhaust tips anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ed||04-25-2001||10:53 PM||||I just did my GT's with Eagle all finish wheel cleaner.  <P>Is that stuff still made? ||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||04-26-2001||07:09 AM||||i just keep them clean in the first place. wipe them off everytime i clean the car.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfixit58||04-26-2001||07:46 AM||||I just used some VERY cheap rubbing compound (Turtle Wax - $2.00 a can). I just slap a gob onto the tip and use a rag like a shoe-shine boy. Seemed to work pretty good.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000012||FieroHarry||04-26-2001||08:22 AM||||Mine was nasty when I first got it.<BR>Used very fine steel wool (for light sanding polyurithane finishes).<BR>Then any metal polish will due....<P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||6
